<!--
  The Google Sheet rebuild, run by launchd. 5 wake ups a week: 16:35, Monday to
  Friday.

  WHAT IT DOES. At 16:35 New York it rewrites the Google Sheet ledger from
  /Users/mtalib/workspace_repos/personal_repo/agentic_trading/data/trading.sqlite. The database is the record; the sheet is a picture
  of it that Mo can open on a phone. Nothing writes to the sheet during the day
  any more, so a broken wifi connection at half past nine in the morning costs
  nothing.

  IT CANNOT TRADE. It reads one file on disk and writes to one Google Sheet. It
  never opens a connection to IB Gateway and has no way to place an order.

  IT IS SAFE TO RUN TWICE. Every tab is cleared over the columns the agent owns
  and rewritten from the top, so a second run in the same evening produces the
  same sheet rather than a doubled one. It never appends.

  Take the last argument out of the program block above, the write flag, and it
  becomes a rehearsal: it works out every row, reads the live sheet to check the
  column headings still line up, prints what it would send, and writes nothing.
  (The flag cannot be spelled out here, because XML forbids two hyphens in a row
  inside a comment.)

  WHAT IT NEEDS. The Google token at /Users/mtalib/workspace_repos/personal_repo/agentic_trading/.secrets/token_personal_drive.json and
  the sheet id in /Users/mtalib/workspace_repos/personal_repo/agentic_trading/config/ledger.json. If either is missing it says so and
  stops without touching anything.

  ARMED ON 2026-09-07 by the hub's ruling. It was run once by hand against the
